{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality carries complementary or superior signal relative to RNA. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to the existing baseline: same profile_setting (singleprofile), same simplicity (no aggregation/fusion), only the modality changes. If image_only substantially outperforms 48.5%, it justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal configurations and tells us the image encoder is the stronger backbone. If it performs similarly or worse, it indicates RNA is the primary signal and we should prioritize RNA encoder upgrades or multiprofile aggregation. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis (modality) before committing budget to more complex multimodal or aggregation variants, making it the highest-information-use next step under a tight budget."
}

